<%# The top-of-funnel explainer, and the page that will become /about (the swap
    is its own task; /about is untouched). Modelled on Calm's landing page: a
    dark starry hero with one big CTA and the product in a phone, then a light
    section with a second phone beside a short feature list.

    Sections, in order:
      1. HERO         what the game is, in one headline and two sentences
      2. NOTIFY       the countdown to the next slate drop, and a notify-me form
      3. HOW TO PLAY  four icon rows beside the scoring phone
      4. CLOSING      the two CTAs again

    NOTHING HERE IS A NEW RULE. Every fact is the v1 rules page's, and every
    number is read from TurfMonsterRules (multipliers, the example entry) or
    NextSlateDrop (the drop instant and its slate key), so this page cannot
    disagree with the rules it summarises. The full rules stay on
    turf_monster_v1_path, and this page links there.

    ENTRY COST LINKS OUT, ALWAYS. The v1 operator rule holds here too: any
    mention of what an entry costs links to getting_started_path.

    THE HERO IS DARK IN BOTH THEMES, on purpose: it is the Calm night sky, so
    its colours are fixed rather than theme tokens, and its text is white on
    both. Everything below the hero is on theme tokens. %>
<% content_for :title, "Turf Monster — Pick 6 NFL Teams, Stack Points" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "NFL pick'em: choose 6 teams, every point they score over the three-week slate counts, times their Turf Score. Underdogs carry the bigger multiplier. The #{NextSlateDrop::LABEL} slate drops Tuesday morning." %>
<% dropped   = NextSlateDrop.dropped? %>
<% remaining = NextSlateDrop.remaining %>
<% top_score = TurfMonsterRules.turf_score_for_rank(1) %>
<% low_score = TurfMonsterRules.turf_score_for_rank(TurfMonsterRules::TEAM_COUNT) %>

<script>
  // Inline for the reason every page-level factory in this app is: importmap
  // modules run AFTER Alpine walks x-data, so a factory defined there is not
  // there yet on a fresh load.

  // The countdown. The server renders the first frame (days/hours/minutes
  // and which state is showing), so the page reads right with JS off; this
  // ticks it every second, stops the interval at zero, and flips the section
  // to "live" at the instant. Hours, minutes and seconds are zero-padded
  // strings, so the tiles keep their width as the digits change.
  window.dropCountdown = function (iso, days, hours, minutes, dropped) {
    var pad = function (n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; };
    return {
      target: Date.parse(iso),
      days: days, hours: pad(hours), minutes: pad(minutes), seconds: '00', dropped: dropped,
      timer: null,
      init: function () {
        this.tick();
        if (!this.dropped) this.timer = setInterval(this.tick.bind(this), 1000);
      },
      destroy: function () { clearInterval(this.timer); },
      tick: function () {
        var s = Math.max(0, Math.floor((this.target - Date.now()) / 1000));
        this.days = Math.floor(s / 86400);
        this.hours = pad(Math.floor((s % 86400) / 3600));
        this.minutes = pad(Math.floor((s % 3600) / 60));
        this.seconds = pad(s % 60);
        if (s <= 0) {
          clearInterval(this.timer);
          this.timer = null;
          this.dropped = true;
        }
      }
    };
  };

  // The notify-me form. SUCCESS ONLY ON A 2xx THE SERVER CONFIRMS: fetch does
  // not reject on an HTTP error, so a 422 or 429 resolves like a 200 would,
  // and the state is read from res.ok and the body, never from "it resolved".
  // Form-encoded, not JSON, so the per-email throttle (which reads Rack's form
  // params) sees the address.
  window.dropNotifyForm = function (initial) {
    return {
      state: initial || 'idle', // 'idle' | 'submitting' | 'done' | 'error'
      error: initial === 'error' ? 'Enter a valid email address.' : '',
      submit: function (event) {
        if (this.state === 'submitting') return;
        var form = event.target;
        var token = document.querySelector('meta[name=csrf-token]');
        this.state = 'submitting';
        this.error = '';
        fetch(form.action, {
          method: 'POST',
          credentials: 'same-origin',
          headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json', 'X-CSRF-Token': token ? token.content : '' },
          body: new URLSearchParams(new FormData(form))
        }).then(function (res) {
          return res.json().catch(function () { return {}; }).then(function (data) {
            if (res.ok && data.ok) { this.state = 'done'; return; }
            this.state = 'error';
            this.error = res.status === 429 ? 'Too many tries. Give it a few minutes and try again.'
                       : (data.error || 'Something went wrong. Try again.');
          }.bind(this));
        }.bind(this)).catch(function () {
          this.state = 'error';
          this.error = 'Could not reach the server. Check your connection and try again.';
        }.bind(this));
      }
    };
  };
</script>

<%# data-test hook: the tests scope their copy assertions to THIS subtree. The
    layout ships site-wide meta that still advertises the World Cup season, so a
    page-wide response.body scan would read the chrome, not the page. %>
<div class="py-4 md:py-8 space-y-16 md:space-y-24" data-test="turf-monster-v2">

  <!-- ========== 1. HERO ========== -->
  <%# Two layered backgrounds: a field of small radial-gradient "stars" over
      the night gradient. Fixed hex on purpose (see the header). %>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl px-6 py-12 md:px-12 md:py-16"
           data-test="v2-hero"
           style="background-image:
             radial-gradient(1px 1px at 12% 18%, #ffffffcc 50%, transparent 51%),
             radial-gradient(1px 1px at 28% 72%, #ffffff99 50%, transparent 51%),
             radial-gradient(1.5px 1.5px at 44% 34%, #ffffffb3 50%, transparent 51%),
             radial-gradient(1px 1px at 63% 12%, #ffffff99 50%, transparent 51%),
             radial-gradient(1px 1px at 78% 58%, #ffffffcc 50%, transparent 51%),
             radial-gradient(1.5px 1.5px at 90% 26%, #ffffff80 50%, transparent 51%),
             radial-gradient(1px 1px at 8% 88%, #ffffff80 50%, transparent 51%),
             radial-gradient(1px 1px at 52% 92%, #ffffff99 50%, transparent 51%),
             linear-gradient(160deg, #0b1026 0%, #18204f 45%, #3a2a6e 80%, #4a3780 100%);">
    <%# From xl the gap tightens to gap-8, which keeps the copy column wide
        enough for the subhead's three lines and gives the laptop behind the
        phone its room. %>
    <div class="grid items-center gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 xl:gap-8">
      <div class="text-center md:text-left">
        <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/25 bg-white/10 text-white text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">NFL 2026</span>
        <%# ONE SENTENCE PER LINE at every width: three block spans, each kept
            whole (whitespace-nowrap), at a size whose longest line, "Stack
            points.", still fits the hero at 375px. %>
        <h1 class="mt-5 text-[2rem] sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-white">
          <span class="block whitespace-nowrap">Pick 6 teams.</span>
          <span class="block whitespace-nowrap">Stack points.</span>
          <span class="block whitespace-nowrap">Get paid.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-white/80 max-w-xl mx-auto md:mx-0" data-test="v2-subhead">
          Choose 6 NFL teams. Every point they score over the three-week slate counts, times their Turf Score. Underdogs carry the bigger multiplier, so a smart longshot beats the favorite.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center md:justify-start">
          <%= render "pages/next_contest_cta", pick: @next_contest, test_id: "v2-hero-cta" %>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# THE PHONE with its caption directly under it, and from xl up a LAPTOP
          behind it, as on Calm's page. Below xl the phone is centered in its
          column; from xl it sits at the column's left so the laptop has room.
          The laptop hangs off the phone's wrapper: its left edge under the
          phone's right third, its top above the phone's, the phone running
          below its base. Drawn at 448px and scaled 1.25 (560px) so the live
          snapshot reads; it runs past the hero's right edge, where the
          section's overflow-hidden clips about a fifth of it, so it never adds
          page width. Absolutely positioned, so it never moves the phone or the
          copy. Below xl it is not drawn: the column leaves too thin a sliver
          beside the phone to read. %>
      <figure class="flex flex-col items-center xl:items-start" data-test="v2-hero-figure">
        <div class="relative">
          <div class="hidden xl:block absolute z-0 left-[66%] -top-14 origin-top-left scale-125" data-test="laptop-anchor">
            <%= render "pages/laptop_lobby", lobby: @lobby, showcase: @live_showcase, live_html: @laptop_live_html %>
          </div>
          <div class="relative z-10 drop-shadow-2xl">
            <%= render layout: "pages/phone_frame", locals: { screen_class: "h-[26.5rem]" } do %>
              <%= render "pages/phone_pick_board", teams: @teams %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="relative z-10 mt-4 w-[17rem] text-center text-xs text-white/70">
          Real cards from the Weeks 1&ndash;3 board.<span class="sr-only"> Behind the phone, a laptop shows the live contests lobby.</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========== 2. NEXT CONTEST / NOTIFY ME ========== -->
  <%# The countdown owns this section's x-data; the form nests inside it so it
      can hide itself once the slate is live. The server picks the first frame
      (style="display:none" on the state that is NOT current), so with JS off
      the right half shows and the numbers are right as of the request. %>
  <section id="notify" class="scroll-mt-24 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center" data-test="v2-notify"
           x-data="dropCountdown('<%= NextSlateDrop.drops_at.utc.iso8601 %>', <%= remaining[:days] %>, <%= remaining[:hours] %>, <%= remaining[:minutes] %>, <%= dropped %>)">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">Next contest</p>

    <div x-show="!dropped" <%= 'style="display: none;"'.html_safe if dropped %>>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-heading mb-3"><%= NextSlateDrop::LABEL %> slate drops Tuesday morning</h2>
      <p class="text-secondary mb-8">
        The board for NFL <%= NextSlateDrop::LABEL %> goes live <%= NextSlateDrop.drops_at.strftime("%A, %B %-d") %> at <%= NextSlateDrop.drops_at.strftime("%-l:%M %p") %> Mountain.
      </p>

      <%# One column: the tiles and the card share max-w-2xl, and the card sits
          mt-8 under the tiles (the tiles partial carries no margin of its own,
          so each call site sets its spacing). %>
      <%= render "pages/drop_countdown_tiles", remaining: remaining %>

      <div class="mt-8">
      <%= render "pages/drop_notify_form", initial: { "ok" => "done", "invalid" => "error" }[@drop_signup_status] || "idle",
                 id_prefix: "drop_signup" %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div x-show="dropped" <%= 'style="display: none;"'.html_safe unless dropped %> data-test="v2-live">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-heading mb-3">The <%= NextSlateDrop::LABEL %> slate is live</h2>
      <p class="text-secondary mb-8">The board is open. Pick your 6 teams before the contest locks.</p>
      <%= link_to "Play now", root_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg shadow-lg shadow-primary/20 text-lg" %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========== 3. HOW TO PLAY ========== -->
  <%# Calm's "What do you get?" layout: a phone on one side, short icon rows on
      the other. Four steps: choose teams, set up the account, points times
      Turf Score, the leaderboard; the copy carries no
      lock timing and no payout timing, for the reasons v1's own comments give. %>
  <section class="rounded-3xl bg-surface border border-subtle px-6 py-12 md:px-12 md:py-16" data-test="v2-how-to-play">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-12 md:grid-cols-2">
      <figure class="order-2 md:order-1 flex flex-col items-center">
        <%= render layout: "pages/phone_frame" do %>
          <%= render "pages/phone_scoring", teams: @teams %>
        <% end %>
        <figcaption class="mt-4 max-w-xs text-center text-xs text-muted">
          Each team&rsquo;s points times its Turf Score. Real teams and Turf Scores; made-up points.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="order-1 md:order-2">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-heading mb-2">How to play</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary mb-8">Four steps. That&rsquo;s the whole game.</p>

        <ul class="space-y-6">
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-primary/15 text-primary" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.8" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 6A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 6 3.75h2.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 10.5 6v2.25a2.25 2.25 0 0 1-2.25 2.25H6a2.25 2.25 0 0 1-2.25-2.25V6ZM3.75 15.75A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 6 13.5h2.25a2.25 2.25 0 0 1 2.25 2.25V18a2.25 2.25 0 0 1-2.25 2.25H6A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 3.75 18v-2.25ZM13.5 6a2.25 2.25 0 0 1 2.25-2.25H18A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 20.25 6v2.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 18 10.5h-2.25a2.25 2.25 0 0 1-2.25-2.25V6ZM13.5 15.75a2.25 2.25 0 0 1 2.25-2.25H18a2.25 2.25 0 0 1 2.25 2.25V18A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 18 20.25h-2.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 13.5 18v-2.25Z"/></svg>
            </span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Choose 6 teams</h3>
              <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Tap 6 teams from the board, then hold to confirm. Each card shows the team&rsquo;s Turf Score (as &ldquo;1.1x Points&rdquo;) and its opponents for all three weeks.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>

          <%# VERIFIED 2026-10-05 against production: the sign-in modal offers
              Google, a Solana wallet (Phantom) and an emailed magic link, and
              web3-only onboarding is on (ENABLE_WEB3_ONLY_ONBOARDING unset, so
              AppFlags defaults it true). A Google or email account gets no
              wallet, so entering takes a linked Phantom wallet for everyone;
              the copy says so. Entry cost links to Getting Started (v1's rule). %>
          <li class="flex gap-4" data-test="v2-account-step">
            <span class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-primary/15 text-primary" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.8" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M21 12a2.25 2.25 0 0 0-2.25-2.25H15a3 3 0 1 1-6 0H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 3 12m18 0v6a2.25 2.25 0 0 1-2.25 2.25H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 1 3 18v-6m18 0V9M3 12V9m18 0a2.25 2.25 0 0 0-2.25-2.25H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 3 9m18 0V6a2.25 2.25 0 0 0-2.25-2.25H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 3 6v3"/></svg>
            </span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Set up your account</h3>
              <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Sign in with Google, email or Phantom. To enter, connect a Phantom wallet and add USDC to cover your entry. The
                <%= link_to "Getting Started guide", getting_started_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %>
                walks you through it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-violet/15 text-violet-ink" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.8" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 18 18 6M6 6l12 12"/></svg>
            </span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Points &times; Turf Score</h3>
              <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed" data-test="v2-turf-score-step">
                Every point a team scores counts for you, multiplied by its Turf Score: <span class="font-mono text-violet-ink"><%= number_with_precision(top_score, precision: 1) %>x</span> for the team projected to score the most, up to <span class="font-mono text-violet-ink"><%= number_with_precision(low_score, precision: 1) %>x</span> for the team projected to score the least.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-primary/15 text-primary" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.8" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 13.125C3 12.504 3.504 12 4.125 12h2.25c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125v6.75C7.5 20.496 6.996 21 6.375 21h-2.25A1.125 1.125 0 0 1 3 19.875v-6.75ZM9.75 8.625c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h2.25c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125v11.25c0 .621-.504 1.125-1.125 1.125h-2.25a1.125 1.125 0 0 1-1.125-1.125V8.625ZM16.5 4.125c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h2.25C20.496 3 21 3.504 21 4.125v15.75c0 .621-.504 1.125-1.125 1.125h-2.25a1.125 1.125 0 0 1-1.125-1.125V4.125Z"/></svg>
            </span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Climb the leaderboard and get paid</h3>
              <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
                As scores come in your entry is re-scored, and the contest page shows where you stand. When the last game is over the standings are final, and payouts go to the wallet you entered from.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-secondary text-sm mt-8">
          Want the details? Read the
          <%= link_to "full rules", turf_monster_v1_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline font-semibold" %>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ========== 4. CLOSING CTA ========== -->
  <section class="text-center pb-8" data-test="v2-closing">
    <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-6">Ready to play?</p>
    <div class="flex justify-center">
      <%= render "pages/next_contest_cta", pick: @next_contest, test_id: "v2-closing-cta" %>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm mt-6">
      Never used a crypto wallet? Start with the
      <%= link_to "Getting Started guide", getting_started_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %>.
    </p>
  </section>

</div>
